{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"agent_message","text":"The disassembly shows the mismatch source precisely: GCC evaluates `lm_dot2` as `add(mul(b.y, a.y), mul(a.x, b.x))`, while several Rust helper calls reversed those SSE destination operands. I’m replacing the hand-expanded dot products and formula multiplications with the exact C/GCC operand order; finite arithmetic remains unchanged, while NaN payload selection will match."}}
